:: ramesh_gate_d4
Ramesh's thermos is at half-capacity, the morning chai consumption on schedule. He looks up from the crossword.

<<dl "\"Kavya didi, itni subah? Pooja se waapas?\"" "Kavya didi, this early? Back from the pooja?">>

He KNOWS. "Kavya" signed out at 4:48 for temple pooja; back at 6:00 is exactly a one-hour prayer visit. The cover holds without you saying anything else.

<<dl "\"Haan, Ramesh ji. Saat din ki pooja. Subah paanch baje.\"" "Yes, Ramesh ji. Seven-day pooja. Five in the morning.">>

<<dl "\"Acchi baat hai. Bhagwaan ka kaam.\"" "Good. God's work.">> He nods with the approving energy of a man who considers early-morning devotion the gold standard of young-woman behaviour. Temple-going girls are the BEST category in the chowkidar's moral taxonomy   devout, responsible, certainly not involved in anything requiring his attention.
\
<<run setup.flag("chowkidar_passed_d4")>>
<<hubreturn>>


